ual Royal St Andrew's Golf tournament.\",\"population_estimate\":8000,\"archetype\":\"coastal_town\",\"coordinator_status\":\"recruiting\",\"route\":\"/town/port-alfred\",\"illustrative\":true},{\"slug\":\"alice\",\"name\":\"Alice\",\"region\":\"university town\",\"status\":\"ghost\",\"render_pct\":0,\"opportunity_potential\":30,\"lat\":-32.7833,\"lng\":26.8333,\"description\":\"Home to the University of Fort Hare — the alma mater of Nelson Mandela, Robert Sobukwe, and Oliver Tambo — Alice is a small Eastern Cape town with an outsized place in African history.\",\"population_estimate\":5000,\"archetype\":\"university_town\",\"coordinator_status\":\"recruiting\",\"route\":\"/town/alice\",\"illustrative\":true},{\"slug\":\"komani\",\"name\":\"Komani\",\"region\":\"interior town\",\"status\":\"ghost\",\"render_pct\":0,\"opportunity_potential\":30,\"lat\":-31.9,\"lng\":26.8833,\"description\":\"Known historically as Queenstown, Komani is a major centre in the Eastern Cape's interior, surrounded by rolling grasslands and rich Xhosa heritage.\",\"population_estimate\":35000,\"archetype\":\"interior_town\",\"coordinator_status\":\"recruiting\",\"route\":\"/town/komani\",\"illustrative\":true},{\"slug\":\"port-st-johns\",\"name\":\"Port St Johns\",\"region\":\"wild coast\",\"status\":\"ghost\",\"render_pct\":0,\"opportunity_potential\":30,\"lat\":-31.6333,\"lng\":29.55,\"description\":\"The gateway to the Wild Coast, Port St John sits at the mouth of the Umzimvubu River where two mountains frame a stunning lagoon. This is raw, unspoiled Africa.\",\"population_estimate\":5000,\"archetype\":\"wild_coast\",\"coordinator_status\":\"recruiting\",\"route\":\"/town/port-st-johns\",\"illustrative\":true},{\"slug\":\"hogsback\",\"name\":\"Hogsback\",\"region\":\"mountain village\",\"status\":\"ghost\",\"render_pct\":0,\"opportunity_potential\":30,\"lat\":-32.5833,\"lng\":26.95,\"description\":\"A mystical mountain village wrapped in indigenous forest and waterfalls, Hogsback is said